Trust Policy Role

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "AllowVPCFlowLogsServiceToAssumeRole",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}

Purpose: This is the Trust Policy (Authentication layer) 
attached to the IAM Role.

Explanation: By default, AWS services cannot touch your resources 
without explicit permission. This statement grants the AWS VPC Flow 
Logs service (vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com) permission to call 
sts:AssumeRole and assume this role.



VPC Flow Logs: Permissions Policy (JSON Policy)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "AllowFlowLogsToCloudWatch",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "logs:CreateLogGroup",
        "logs:CreateLogStream",
        "logs:PutLogEvents",
        "logs:DescribeLogGroups",
        "logs:DescribeLogStreams"
      ],
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}
Purpose: This is the Permissions Policy (Authorization layer) attached inside the IAM Role.

Explanation:

logs:CreateLogGroup & logs:CreateLogStream: 
Allows VPC Flow Logs to automatically generate log groups and individual
log streams if they do not already exist.

logs:PutLogEvents: Authorizes the service to write and deliver the actual 
captured network metadata packets into CloudWatch.

logs:DescribeLogGroups & logs:DescribeLogStreams: 
Allows the service to query CloudWatch to verify where to send the stream.

Resource: "*": Allows these actions across the CloudWatch Logs service endpoint.